":"support.contact_derivatives","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Derives the value and slope conditions from derivatives of the contact function, with a separate right-hand expansion at zero. The origin argument retains contact at zero when zero belongs to the support and the zero-field identity q(0)=0.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.contact_derivatives"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=short&passage=contact&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&paper=short&passage=contact"},{"ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/passages/first-variation","stage":"expository","anchor":"first-variation","content_span":{"start_byte":25223,"end_byte":26865,"start_line":590,"end_line":625},"section_ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sections/104","section_title":"Why the SK order parameter has no gaps","claim_refs":["sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.first_variation"],"evidence_class":"source_argument","treatments":[{"claim_id":"support.first_variation","kinds":["statement","explanation"],"rationale":"States the admissible one-sided derivative formula and explains the separate penalty and reoptimised-control contributions. Nonnegativity of the derivative requires a minimiser; the cited formula itself applies to admissible coefficients and feasible directions.","claim_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.first_variation"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acb